      "content": "# Authentication Module Guide\n\n## Introduction\nWelcome to the Authentication Module Guide. This document provides a comprehensive overview of our new Authentication module, designed to help developers integrate secure authentication mechanisms into their applications.\n\n## Table of Contents\n1. [Overview](#overview)\n2. [Authentication Flow](#authentication-flow)\n3. [Supported Authentication Methods](#supported-authentication-methods)\n4. [Implementing Authentication](#implementing-authentication)\n5. [Security Best Practices](#security-best-practices)\n6. [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting)\n7. [FAQs](#faqs)\n8. [References](#references)\n\n## Overview\nThe Authentication Module offers a robust and flexible solution for managing user authentication and authorization in your applications. It supports various authentication methods, including OAuth, SAML, and custom token-based authentication.\n\n## Authentication Flow\nThe authentication flow consists of the following steps:\n1. User submits credentials (username and password).\n2. The system validates the credentials against the user database.\n3. If valid, the system generates an authentication token.\n4. The application uses the token to authenticate subsequent requests.\n\n## Supported Authentication Methods\nThe Authentication Module supports the following authentication methods:\n- **OAuth**:",
